explanation:
The domain for the password length has three equivalence partitions:
• passwords too short {0, 1, …, 4, 5}
• passwords OK {6, 7, …, 11, 12}
• passwords too long {13, 14, …}
To achieve full 3-value BVA coverage we need to test: 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 11, 12, 13, 14.
Since 2-value BVA is already covered, lengths 0, 5, 6, 12 and 13 have already been tested.
So the additional lengths needed to move from 2-value to 3-value are: 1, 4, 7, 11 and 14.
Thus a), b), c) are not correct; d) is correct.
